{"id":"phishing","title":"Phishing and social engineering","subject":"Cybersecurity","label":"Cybersecurity","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":163,"duration":162.81,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":462,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The message","start":0,"end":11.625},{"id":"explain","title":"The trick","start":11.625,"end":40.505},{"id":"explain2","title":"Warning signs","start":40.505,"end":72.055},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":72.055,"end":97.635},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":97.635,"end":107.685},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":107.685,"end":114.915},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":114.915,"end":136.235},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":136.235,"end":162.81}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.06,"text":"Hello, I'm Kora. A message says your account will close unless you click now.","w":[0.54,1.02,1.24,2.16,2.26,2.66,2.92,3.12,3.46,3.64,4.12,4.42,4.56,4.8]},{"s":0,"a":5.36,"b":11.2,"text":"Is it real? Today we look at phishing and social engineering, and how to spot the trick before you act.","w":[5.4,5.54,5.68,6.52,6.88,7.02,7.22,7.38,7.76,7.92,8.32,9.26,9.4,9.54,9.68,9.98,10.1,10.38,10.68,10.92]},{"s":1,"a":12.05,"b":19.11,"text":"Social engineering attacks the person, not the computer. It uses trust, fear, or curiosity to make you act.","w":[12.14,12.5,13.06,13.5,13.62,14.52,14.74,14.84,15.78,15.96,16.28,17.04,17.46,17.6,18.3,18.42,18.58,18.82]},{"s":1,"a":19.41,"b":26.29,"text":"Phishing is a fake message that pretends to be someone you trust. Its aim is to steal your passwords, your money, or your codes.","w":[19.44,19.84,19.96,20.16,20.46,20.84,21,21.4,21.52,21.68,21.98,22.14,23.02,23.28,23.48,23.6,23.74,24.04,24.2,25.04,25.24,25.58,25.68,25.86]},{"s":1,"a":26.59,"b":30.01,"text":"Phishing arrives by email. By text, it is called smishing.","w":[26.68,27.04,27.46,27.72,28.44,28.66,29.06,29.18,29.28,29.58]},{"s":1,"a":30.31,"b":34.49,"text":"By phone call, it is called vishing. It also arrives on social media.","w":[30.34,30.56,30.86,31.3,31.42,31.58,31.94,32.9,33.02,33.32,33.72,33.84,34.16]},{"s":1,"a":34.79,"b":40.08,"text":"The message may look official, but the request is the clue. Stop and ask what it wants you to do.","w":[34.82,34.94,35.3,35.48,35.68,36.5,36.64,36.78,37.34,37.48,37.6,38.42,38.78,38.96,39.18,39.32,39.42,39.62,39.74,39.84]},{"s":2,"a":40.93,"b":44.67,"text":"Watch for urgency or fear. Watch for an offer too good to be true.","w":[40.98,41.26,41.48,41.96,42.12,42.98,43.22,43.36,43.52,43.8,43.98,44.16,44.26,44.38]},{"s":2,"a":44.97,"b":48.97,"text":"Check the sender address and the link. A small wrong letter is a warning.","w":[45,45.24,45.38,45.74,46.26,46.36,46.48,47.22,47.38,47.76,48.04,48.4,48.52,48.58]},{"s":2,"a":49.27,"b":55.43,"text":"Be careful if it asks for a password, a PIN, or a one-time code. Treat unexpected attachments as dangerous.","w":[49.27,49.44,49.9,50.07,50.24,50.52,50.75,50.87,51.44,51.55,51.84,52.01,52.12,52.64,52.98,53.32,53.95,54.63,54.8]},{"s":2,"a":55.73,"b":58.11,"text":"So stop. Do not click.","w":[55.8,56.42,57.28,57.46,57.74]},{"s":2,"a":58.41,"b":61.88,"text":"And remember, touching systems without permission is illegal.","w":[58.48,58.62,59.56,59.98,60.4,60.74,61.32,61.46]},{"s":2,"a":62.18,"b":66.99,"text":"Check through the official app or the phone number you already know. Report it and delete it.","w":[62.22,62.44,62.66,62.78,63.26,63.8,63.96,64.08,64.3,64.58,64.78,65.08,65.68,66.1,66.34,66.46,66.78]},{"s":2,"a":67.29,"b":71.63,"text":"Never share a one-time code with anyone. A real bank never asks for it.","w":[67.29,67.65,68.01,68.13,68.68,68.98,69.28,69.76,69.88,70.18,70.48,70.85,71.15,71.39]},{"s":3,"a":72.48,"b":76.4,"text":"Here is a fake message. Your account will be closed in twenty four hours.","w":[72.52,72.72,72.84,72.94,73.22,74,74.24,74.58,74.74,74.86,75.26,75.4,75.74,75.94]},{"s":3,"a":76.7,"b":79.98,"text":"Verify here. Now find three warning signs.","w":[76.74,77.3,78.2,78.5,78.84,79.16,79.52]},{"s":3,"a":80.28,"b":86.24,"text":"First, the deadline creates fear and urgency. Second, the threat of closure pushes you to act fast.","w":[80.36,80.78,80.92,81.38,81.82,82.14,82.3,83.28,84.02,84.2,84.44,84.56,84.98,85.3,85.44,85.62,85.8]},{"s":3,"a":86.54,"b":91.75,"text":"Third, verify here is a link you did not expect, instead of the official app you already use.","w":[86.56,86.86,87.64,87.86,88,88.08,88.3,88.48,88.66,88.86,89.68,90.02,90.1,90.24,90.7,90.84,91,91.42]},{"s":3,"a":92.05,"b":97.21,"text":"The safe move is to stop, not click, open the official app, and check there.","w":[92.06,92.26,92.58,92.9,93.02,93.18,94.06,94.36,95.2,95.46,95.6,96.08,96.58,96.72,96.96]},{"s":4,"a":98.06,"b":103.4,"text":"Quick check. A text says you have won a prize and must send your one-time code to claim it.","w":[98.06,98.41,98.81,98.93,99.22,99.51,99.74,100.03,100.27,100.38,100.73,100.96,101.25,101.54,101.83,102.36,102.65,102.82,103.17]},{"s":4,"a":103.7,"b":104.57,"text":"What should you do?","w":[103.74,103.92,104.12,104.26]},{"s":4,"a":105.02,"b":107.26,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[105.04,105.38,105.62,105.74,106.04,106.78,106.94]},{"s":5,"a":108.11,"b":114.49,"text":"Do not send it. Delete and report the message, because a real prize or bank never needs your one-time code.","w":[108.11,108.29,108.52,108.82,109.06,109.47,109.71,110.12,110.35,110.89,111.36,111.48,111.77,112.13,112.3,112.6,112.95,113.31,113.6,114.14]},{"s":6,"a":115.34,"b":122.63,"text":"One mistake is trusting a message because it looks official. Avoid that by checking through the official app or phone number you already know.","w":[115.48,115.64,116.12,116.26,116.72,116.8,117.48,117.76,117.86,118.16,119.16,119.48,119.7,119.88,120.2,120.4,120.54,121.02,121.24,121.38,121.6,121.84,122.04,122.36]},{"s":6,"a":122.93,"b":127.25,"text":"Another mistake is clicking before you think. Avoid that by stopping first.","w":[123.02,123.34,123.88,124.06,124.46,124.74,124.88,125.64,125.98,126.22,126.38,126.8]},{"s":6,"a":127.55,"b":131.19,"text":"A third mistake is sharing a one-time code to prove who you are.","w":[127.55,127.66,128,128.45,128.61,129.06,129.17,129.68,129.96,130.13,130.46,130.69,130.91]},{"s":6,"a":131.49,"b":135.81,"text":"Avoid that by remembering that no real bank or service will ever ask for it.","w":[131.56,131.94,132.24,132.44,132.96,133.18,133.44,133.74,134.14,134.34,134.74,134.98,135.3,135.52,135.74]},{"s":7,"a":136.66,"b":141.07,"text":"Remember three things. Social engineering attacks the person, not the computer.","w":[136.72,137.12,137.34,138.28,138.7,139.18,139.56,139.66,140.32,140.54,140.64]},{"s":7,"a":141.37,"b":145.13,"text":"Phishing fakes trust to steal passwords, money, or codes.","w":[141.44,141.82,142.18,142.66,142.82,143.16,144,144.46,144.62]},{"s":7,"a":145.43,"b":150.92,"text":"Stop, do not click, check through an official app or number, then report and delete.","w":[145.6,146.38,146.54,146.78,147.44,147.7,147.92,148.02,148.54,148.84,149,149.76,149.96,150.48,150.6]},{"s":7,"a":151.22,"b":156.51,"text":"Top tip: never share a one-time code, because a real bank never asks for it.","w":[151.22,151.49,151.84,152.25,152.66,152.8,153.42,153.83,154.38,154.52,154.86,155.2,155.62,155.96,156.24]},{"s":7,"a":156.81,"b":162.21,"text":"Well done today, and keep practising these habits with Knowzone, because you will spot the trick sooner.","w":[156.86,157.12,157.36,157.96,158.12,158.36,158.92,159.14,159.48,159.68,160.5,160.78,160.9,161.1,161.4,161.54,161.86]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"The message","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Account will close unless you click now"},{"at":5.26,"kind":"text","text":"Is it real? Spot the trick before you act"}]},{"at":11.8,"heading":"The trick","items":[{"at":11.95,"kind":"term","text":"Social engineering","detail":"Attacks the person, not the computer; uses trust, fear, curiosity"},{"at":19.31,"kind":"term","text":"Phishing","detail":"Fake message pretending to be trusted; steals passwords, money, codes"},{"at":26.49,"kind":"term","text":"Smishing","detail":"Phishing by text message"},{"at":30.21,"kind":"term","text":"Vishing","detail":"Phishing by phone call"},{"at":34.69,"kind":"text","text":"Look official? The request is the clue. Stop and ask."}]},{"at":40.68,"heading":"Warning signs","items":[{"at":40.83,"kind":"text","text":"Urgency or fear; offer too good to be true"},{"at":44.87,"kind":"text","text":"Check sender address and link; small wrong letter"},{"at":49.17,"kind":"text","text":"Password/PIN/code request; unexpected attachment"},{"at":55.63,"kind":"text","text":"Stop. Do not click."}]},{"at":58.16,"heading":"Safe response","items":[{"at":58.31,"kind":"text","text":"Touching systems without permission is illegal"},{"at":62.08,"kind":"text","text":"Check official app or known number; report and delete"},{"at":67.19,"kind":"text","text":"Never share a one-time code; real bank never asks"}]},{"at":72.23,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":72.38,"kind":"text","text":"Fake message: account closes in 24 hours"},{"at":76.6,"kind":"text","text":"Find three warning signs"},{"at":80.18,"kind":"text","text":"1 Deadline: urgency  2 Closure threat: fear"},{"at":86.44,"kind":"text","text":"3 'Verify here' link unexpected; not official app"},{"at":91.95,"kind":"text","text":"Safe: stop, do not click, open official app, check"}]},{"at":97.64,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":97.64,"kind":"question","text":"A text says you have won a prize and must send your one-time code to claim it. What should you do?"}]},{"at":107.86,"heading":"The answer","items":[{"at":108.01,"kind":"text","text":"Do not send it."},{"at":108.01,"kind":"text","text":"Delete and report; real prize/bank never needs code"}]},{"at":115.09,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":115.24,"kind":"wrong","text":"Trusting a message because it looks official"},{"at":122.83,"kind":"wrong","text":"Clicking before you think"},{"at":127.45,"kind":"wrong","text":"Sharing a one-time code to prove who you are"}]},{"at":136.41,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":136.56,"kind":"text","text":"Social engineering attacks the person, not computer"},{"at":141.27,"kind":"text","text":"Phishing fakes trust to steal passwords, money, codes"},{"at":145.33,"kind":"text","text":"Stop, don't click, check official app/number, report/delete"},{"at":151.12,"kind":"tip","text":"Never share a one-time code; a real bank never asks"}]}],"check":{"at":107.51,"seconds":10,"question":"A text says you have won a prize and must send your one-time code to claim it. What should you do?","answer":"Do not send it. Delete and report the message; a real prize or bank never needs your one-time code."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}